            <ArticleTitle>[Comparison of the antagonistic effects of 6 beta-naltrexol and naltrexone against morphine analgesia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>578-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="AIM" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To compare the antagonistic effects of 6 beta-naltrexol and naltrexone against morphine analgesia.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The effects of 6 beta-naltrexol and naltrexone against morphine analgesia were observed in mouse heat radiant tail-flick assay and in mouse (55 +/- 1) degrees C hot plate test. The displacement of 6 beta-naltrexol and naltrexone on binding to CHO-mu receptor was observed by radioligand binding study.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">6 beta-naltrexol antagonized morphine analgesia but the potency was (6.1 +/- 1.7)% that of naltrexone. The effective duration of 6 beta-naltrexol was 3-4 times that of naltrexone and the peak time of the response was about 0.5-1 h after s.c. equivalent efficacy dose (ED95) in two models. Like naltrexone, 6 beta-naltrexol was effective by oral administration and the potency ratio of p.o./s.c. was 1/3. As an antagonist to opioid receptor, the displacement of 6 beta-naltrexol was about 12.5% that of naltrexone, which was almost in agreement with the efficacies against morphine analgesia in mouse.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Compared with naltrexone, 6 beta-naltrexol was less potent but duration was longer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
